rule: ELIM-G-20
A function chosen at runtime is a tag, and each use of it dispatches on the
tag; nothing is allocated.
CHECK-DAG: chr 97 => jump j{{[0-9]+}}(0:Int)
CHECK-DAG: _ => jump j{{[0-9]+}}(1:Int)
A list chosen at runtime passes its tag and the atoms of every alternative,
undefined for the alternatives not taken.
CHECK-DAG: 0:Int => jump j{{[0-9]+}}(0:Int, undef:Int, undef:Int)
CHECK-DAG: _ => jump j{{[0-9]+}}(1:Int, %{{[0-9]+}}, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-NOT: Main.len
